## Approach

Post-parse step in `post_parse_sequence`, matching the health/components pattern. Re-parses source files with tree-sitter to access ASTs (tree is dropped by `parse_single_file` before post_parse runs — re-parse cost is ~ms/file, negligible vs FFT encoding cost). The HRR core (FFT, vector ops, codebook, RNG) is ported verbatim from the spike's `hrr.rs`; the encoder is adapted from `hrr-spike.rs::encode_hrr`. Codebook entries are durable (survive reindex), vectors are ephemeral (recomputed from source + codebook on full reindex).

Alternative considered: encoding inline during `parse_single_file` while the tree is still alive. Rejected because it requires threading the codebook and ParserPool through parse signatures, and breaks the architectural pattern where all derived data (health, components, pagerank) is computed in `post_parse_sequence`.

